# Native HTML/JS computer

This is a **standalone JS-native machine** (HTML5 Canvas games, no general CSS
engine). JavaScript bytecode is the ISA. There is no hidden CPU, no
browser-on-FPGA, no Linux. BASIC sibling = method only, not pins or tokens.

**Forbidden as the machine:** dukpy / Duktape / V8 / QuickJS / Node / Chrome;
Z80 / RISC-V / MicroBlaze / any soft CPU; executing JS **source** as one giant
RTL FSM (bytecode is what the chip fetches).

```
LOAD "NAME.HTML" → edit (line numbers = HTML) → RUN
  → always compile current HTML → in-memory ProgramImage (code + ASET)
  → JMR VM. Chrome = authoring only.
```

**Compile-on-RUN:** editor HTML is truth. No `.JSH` / `.JSB` sidecar. Compile
errors use HTML line numbers. Missing path → loud `?NH` (tracked debt, never
done). ESC is machine BREAK to READY — titles must not steal it.

**Three rooms:** **BRAM** = dual FB + code + heap (do not shrink for a small
die; ASIC ~30 mm², ~1 MB-class SRAM). **µSD** = disk (`NAME.HTML`). **External
4 MB SRAM** = ASET art only (`addr[20:0]`, 16-bit, `we`/`req`/`ack`; FPGA =
DDR3 behind that port; SIM = model behind the same port). No `NAME.DAT`. No
64K BASIC house. Do not pack/downscale/quantize Donkey sheets into code BRAM.

**Files:** `storage/*.HTML` only. `storage/games_*` = upstream, not DIR/card.
`NAME.JS` is not a twin of `NAME.HTML`. Order of rungs: `python-first-parity`.
FPGA-SIM default: `never-fake-fpga-sim`.
